[style name="our style"]
join renko left
renko: I don’t know how much more of this I can take. Between all these trials, and puzzles, and that creature chasing after me.
renko: But I have to keep going. I know she’s waiting for me.
unknown: I see your resolve is being tested. Has this temporal space grown to be too much of a burden on you?
renko: Great, another weirdo is here. I don’t have time for this. Just hurry up and get on with it.
join eiki right
eiki: Very well. I am Eiki Shiki, Yamaxanadu. And do not worry, I already know your name, Renko Usami.
renko: Huh? How did you-
renko: You know what, nevermind. You already knowing my name is the least of my worries.
renko: But wow that’s a pretty big mouthful of a name for you. Did I hear you correctly? A Yama? Did I die or something?
renko: Are you hear to send me to my own personal hell, or am I already in it?
eiki: While typically this would be the case, no you are not dead. So you have no need to fear for your soul…at the moment.
renko: Comforting…
renko: Well if you’re not here to judge me are you here to help me or just be another obstacle?
eiki: To aid you, in a sense.
renko: You gonna help me solve my next trial or?
eiki: No, my aid is more self-reflective. Just truthfully answer my questions. How do you feel about putting yourself in danger for your friend?
renko: What kinda…whatever. I guess, I’m a bit frustrated and maybe a tad…worried for Merry, but I know I need to push through.
eiki: I see. Next question, if you could leave right now, would you?
renko: Would, would Merry come with me?
eiki: No.
renko: Then absolutely not, I would never leave her behind.
eiki: Very noble indeed.
eiki: One final question, if you could trade places with Merry and she could escape but you would not, would you?
renko: What kinda…of course! Merry might be upset, but if she was safe then it’s fine.
eiki: Hmm, I understand.
eiki: By my judgement, your heart leans towards white.
renko: Is, is that good?
eiki: Black and white are neither good nor bad. Not pure nor wicked. These two aspects are just a balance and mirror of each other. My judgement is just what your soul exists as.
eiki: But this does mean you're ready for your next trial and your inevitable final confrontation with her.
renko: Wait, her? Do you mean Merry?!
eiki: No, I mean the entity behind all of this.
renko: You know who that is?!
eiki: Yes, but the knowledge of such would not help you.
renko: Tch…
eiki: It would be best for the best if you just proceeded onward. But I will offer you just a smidge of advice.
eiki: Continuing to develop your powers of observation would be wise. You will need it for the upcoming tests.
renko: Okay…
